.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAP-DELETE-EGRESS-LIMIT 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eap-delete-egress-limit \- return an outside site to the default egress limits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eap delete-egress-limit
\fB\-\-site\fR \fIhost\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes the limit set for one site with
.BR euclid-cli-eap-set-egress-limit (1),
so it's held to
.I euclid.modules.eap.egress.default
again. What's in flight to the site, and a block it asked for, stay
counted: forgetting them would let the site be overrun the moment this
is run. Fails with HTTP 404 if the site has no limit of its own. The
caller must be an administrator.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-site " " \fIhost\fR
The site's host name.
.SH OUTPUT
The site and the default limits now in force for it, as JSON.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eap delete-egress-limit --site downloads.example.com
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eap (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-set-egress-limit (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-list-egress-sites (1)
